# NFL Week 2 ticket construction (2026)

## Decision (explicit)

Weeks 1–3 step5 may **PRIOR_SEASON_FILL** face L5/L10 from last year's boxes for display / list consistency (`l5_sample_n` stays current-season). That is not ticket eligibility.

Ticket Gate70 still needs current-season depth via `nfl_current_season_l5_ok` (rejects `PRIOR_*` / `THIN_*` / `l5_sample_n < 5`). Do **not** flip `NFL_WIDER_WINDOW_TICKET_L5_ENABLED` to manufacture READY. Call `assert_nfl_ticket_l5_source(...)` before any cache-based L5 for tickets; it raises `NflWiderWindowTicketBlocked`.

Sit-list and n=1 hand-checks (Shough OT caution, Bateman DNP-zero fade, Monangai hard-line fades, etc.) live **outside** `nfl_standard_ticket_eligible`. Any path that bypasses the hand-checked list bypasses that judgment with no flag — same shape as the unguarded manual-submit door.

## n=1 hand-check shelf life

An n=1 hand-check is a verdict on **player + prop + a specific line at a specific moment**, not a durable rating on the player. When the board moves, the old line’s verdict expires.

Durable store: **player + prop + Week-1 (or sample) actual**. Line comparison is always done **fresh** against whatever Goblin/Standard faces are live now. Marks clearing **O25.5** vs a 42-yard Week 1 game does **not** auto-clear **24.5 / 19.5 / 9.5** — re-ask gap-to-line for each posted number (trivial arithmetic, but required; an easier line changes what “clears comfortably” means).

Never auto-substitute the nearest face to keep a ticket READY. Leave incomplete until each live line is re-checked against the durable actual.

Do **not** hard-code checked lines (25.5, 36.5, …) into this rule or into builders as permanent eligibility — those numbers go stale the same way a day-prior `utils` copy did.

## READY slips

An NFL PrizePicks slip may print **READY** only when `ticket_source` is hand-check (`assert_nfl_ready_source`). Algorithmic keep-packer / wider-window fills must not claim READY or invite submit.

